---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Institute · ITNRI" description="Introduction to the International Translational Neuroscience Research Institute (ITNRI).">
  <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold">The Institute</h1>
  <p class="mt-2 text-neutral-500">International Translational Neuroscience Research Institute (ITNRI)</p>

  <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-6">
    <figure class="text-center">
      <img src="/itnri-logo.png" alt="ITNRI logo" class="h-28 w-28 rounded-full object-cover" />
      <figcaption class="mt-2 text-sm text-neutral-500">ITNRI</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <figure class="text-center">
      <img src="/zcmu-logo.png" alt="Zhejiang Chinese Medical University logo" class="h-28 w-28 rounded-full object-cover" />
      <figcaption class="mt-2 text-sm text-neutral-500">Zhejiang Chinese Medical University</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>

  <p class="mt-8 leading-relaxed text-neutral-700 dark:text-neutral-300">
    The International Translational Neuroscience Research Institute (ITNRI) is a neuroscience
    research institute at Zhejiang Chinese Medical University (ZCMU) in Hangzhou, China.
    It is directed by Distinguished Professor Vladimir Parpura, a Cheung Kong Scholar and
    Kun Peng Action Expert.
  </p>
  <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-neutral-700 dark:text-neutral-300">
    ITNRI's defining discovery is the astrocyte–neuron glutamate-mediated signalling pathway,
    known as gliotransmission. This led to the concept of the tripartite synapse, in which
    astrocytes, by releasing a gliotransmitter, can modulate synaptic transmission and
    plasticity. The institute interfaces neuroscience with nanoscience and nanotechnology,
    neurochemistry, synthetic biology and biomedical engineering.
  </p>
  <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-neutral-500">
    <!-- TODO: Replace this page with the institute's official introduction, history and mission statement when available. -->
    Note: This is a short introduction drawn from the director's CV. Replace it with ITNRI's
    official introduction when available.
  </p>
</Layout>
